  "question": {
    "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></math> is a point on the parabola whose ordinate equals its abscissa. A normal is drawn to the parabola at <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> to meet it again at <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></math> is the focus of the parabola, then the product of the slopes of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q </mi></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
